WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:09.420
Armed conflict in the South China Sea is
certainly unlikely, but it can't be ruled

00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:14.910
out. Nationalist sentiment has been
inflamed in China, the Philippines, and

00:00:14.910 --> 00:00:18.480
Vietnam, and that can put pressure on
leadership in those countries to act in

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:20.580
provocative and unconstructive ways.

00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:25.890
Secondly, severe power imbalances in the
region between China on the one hand and

00:00:25.890 --> 00:00:29.429
Southeast Asian states on the other are
not conducive to strategic stability.

00:00:29.429 --> 00:00:34.260
Those imbalances make China more likely
to resort to the use of coercion or even

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:37.680
force, especially if Beijing believes
that America's commitment to its

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:43.350
partners in the region is not credible.
And lastly, China has been acting

00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:48.300
dangerously and even recklessly in the
South China Sea. It has harassed US

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:52.800
military vessels and aircraft, it has
tried to deny the resupply of Philippine

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:56.550
marines stationed in the South China Sea,
fishing boats have been sunk, and it has

00:00:56.550 --> 00:01:03.059
built artificial islands. Thus far, major
incidents have been avoided, cooler heads

00:01:03.059 --> 00:01:05.939
have prevailed, but we simply can't count on
that going forward.

00:01:05.939 --> 00:01:10.200
Do you think the South China Sea is
worth fighting for?

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:13.590
Let us know in the comments, and also let
us know what other topics you want

00:01:13.590 --> 00:01:15.210
AEI scholars to cover in 60 seconds.

